   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "widgets_values": [
    "HaDeS MOSS Suite - Turbo 8 steps + Upscale x2 (the second video tutorial)\n\n1. Generate: MOSS-Image Base with HaDeS Turbo 8-steps v1.0, 8 steps, CFG 1, euler / simple, 1024 px.\n   The first video's fisherman (seed 1013). The MOSS Latent's seed feeds both samplers\n   (fixed: set its after run to randomize for new images).\n\n2. Upscale x2: RealESRGAN x2 doubles the image to 2048 in about a second. Nothing is redrawn.\n\n3. Upscale x2 + MOSS pass: VAE Encode and a second MOSS KSampler with the same turbo at denoise 0.25\n   redraw the fine detail the upscaler smooths (skin pores, beard hairs), about 11 s at 2048 on an RTX 5090.\n   Denoise 0.40 adds a little more and changes the image a little more.\n   To skip it: right-click the group > Set Group Nodes to Never.\n\nSuite Telemetry reads every info output, checks the settings against the measurements and feeds the\n   Image Savers' metadata. With two samplers, the PNGs' A1111 parameters are the first sampler's\n   (the 1024 image); connect a second Telemetry to primary_stage_metadata to pick another stage.\n\nModels: RealESRGAN_x2plus.pth in models/upscale_models, the turbo LoRA in models/loras.\nMeasurements: tools/RESULTS.md in the HaDeS MOSS Suite."
   ],
   "properties": {}
  }
